📁 CloudFormation Template

The CloudFormation template was created at:

/root/xfusion-priority-stack.yml

The template defines the required AWS infrastructure as code.

🚀 Deploying the Stack
1. Validate the template
aws cloudformation validate-template \
  --template-body file:///root/xfusion-priority-stack.yml \
  --region us-east-1

Expected result:

Capabilities:
CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM
2. Create the CloudFormation stack
aws cloudformation create-stack \
  --stack-name xfusion-priority-stack \
  --template-body file:///root/xfusion-priority-stack.yml \
  --capabilities CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM \
  --region us-east-1
3. Check stack status
aws cloudformation describe-stacks \
  --stack-name xfusion-priority-stack \
  --region us-east-1 \
  --query "Stacks[0].StackStatus"

Expected:

CREATE_COMPLETE
🔄 Stack Management

CloudFormation manages all resources defined in the template as a single stack.

To view stack resources:

aws cloudformation list-stack-resources \
  --stack-name xfusion-priority-stack \
  --region us-east-1

To delete the stack:

aws cloudformation delete-stack \
  --stack-name xfusion-priority-stack \
  --region us-east-1
🔐 IAM Capabilities

Because the CloudFormation template creates an IAM role, the stack requires:

CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM

Without it, CloudFormation returns:

InsufficientCapabilitiesException

Therefore, the deployment command includes:

--capabilities CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM
⚠️ Troubleshooting
Template validation error

Validate the template before deployment:

aws cloudformation validate-template \
  --template-body file:///root/xfusion-priority-stack.yml \
  --region us-east-1
Stack rollback

If deployment fails:

aws cloudformation describe-stack-events \
  --stack-name xfusion-priority-stack \
  --region us-east-1 \
  --output table

This helps identify which resource caused the failure.

Stack already exists

If you receive:

AlreadyExistsException

check the existing stack:

aws cloudformation describe-stacks \
  --stack-name xfusion-priority-stack \
  --region us-east-1
📚 Key Learnings
CloudFormation provides Infrastructure as Code.
YAML templates can define AWS infrastructure.
A CloudFormation stack manages related resources together.
validate-template helps detect template problems before deployment.
IAM resources may require CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM.
CloudFormation automatically handles resource creation and dependencies.
Stack events are useful for troubleshooting failed deployments.
